  "document": {
    "abstract": "THE event of the first six months of 1928 that attracted the greatest public attention was, of course, the sound or talking motion picture. The technical press has also paid considerable attention to sound production to the exclusion of other familiar subjects. The amateur motion picture is beginning to take a prominent part in the literature, and as this is an attractive field of endeavor for the inventor a large number of technical articles have been published. In general, the literature of motion pictures has taken a great increase during the last few months, so great an increase in fact that in making up this report some thought had to be given to the subject of economy of space, or otherwise it would get out of reasonable bounds.",
